                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Finland/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kagey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-06T18:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1922—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 6—noon.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Referring to the Department’s circular through Paris, April 21, noon. Finnish
                    Minister at Washington has been instructed to negotiate with World War Foreign
                    Debt Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kagey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
